<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold prices seen up on fresh demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold prices seen up on fresh demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to rise slightly this week on fresh demand sparked by what dealers said were relatively low rates.</p>
<p>&quot;Gold prices are down and these are good levels to buy at,&quot; dealer M.S. Imran said. &quot;Gold prices have gained in the international market and will also rise slightly in the domestic market on fresh demand.&quot;</p>
<p>Silver prices are likely to remain steady, dealers said.</p>
<p>Weekly prices:</p>
<p>						     Monday    August 11</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams 4,406     4,410</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		 6,000     6,000</p>
<p>($1=40.62 rupees)</p>
